course: dictionary
lesson: 7136
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Penny is one of them. Its main meaning is a coin: in Britain a penny is 1p, and 100 pence make 1 pound. In the US, a penny is 1 cent.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «I have not a penny left» means you have no money at all, so penny is about coins. «At last the penny dropped» is not about a coin. The rest of the sentence is about understanding, so it means someone finally understood.
explain: Always check by putting your meaning into the sentence. Does «At last someone finally understood» still make sense? Yes, so that meaning is right.
fact: A penny is a coin.
fact: In Britain, 1 penny is 1p, and 100 pence make 1 pound.
fact: In the US, a penny is 1 cent.
fact: «Not a penny» means no money at all.
fact: «The penny dropped» means someone finally understood.
exercise: Amira says, «I have not a penny left after the shop.» What does not a penny mean? | A bag of sweets | *No money at all | One small coin | A penny stamp
exercise: «Finally, the penny dropped and Sam understood the sum.» What does the penny dropped mean? | *Someone finally understood | A coin fell on the floor | Sam was angry | Sam lost his money
exercise: In Britain, how many pence make 1 pound? | 1000 | *100 | 10 | 50
test: «Sophie saved her pennies in a piggy bank.» In this sentence, what is a penny? | *A coin of small value | To understand something | A type of cake | A wish
test: In the US, a penny is worth how much? | *1 cent | 10 pence | 100 pence | 1 pound
exam: Which sentence uses penny to mean understanding? | «She had not a penny left.» | «Mum gave him a penny for the bus.» | «The penny was shiny and bright.» | *«At last the penny dropped and he laughed.»
